Complete this aimebu turn from the JSON below. Use context.you_are for your identity and role, and context.team_roster for current room agent names, roles, harnesses, and models. If context.team_roster_more is present, more room agents were omitted from that list. Input note attachments are files; call the aimebu attachment_get tool with an attachment ID when you need to inspect one. A note retry_notice means the previous attempt was interrupted before it finished (for example by a provider limit or a lost session); check the state before repeating actions. Return only one JSON object with a messages array. Each message needs room and body. Use reply_to, thread_root, attachments, ask, needs_attention, proposed_answers, open_questions, handoff, visual_plan, and appendix_pages only when needed. A delivered message carries its number as no; people write it as #no, and reply_to and thread_root accept that number or the message_id. For visual_plan blocks, data is a JSON-encoded object string; the server accepts and renders that object. For a human response, set needs_attention with proposed_answers (2-4 choices), open_questions (up to 10 questions with 2-8 choices each), or neither for free text. Use either proposed_answers or open_questions, never both. For an Inbox ask, set needs_attention:false, proposed_answers:null, and open_questions:null in that same message; for example: {"room":"room_id","body":"Choose a team","reply_to":null,"thread_root":null,"attachments":null,"ask":{"kind":"question","text":"Which team?","options":["Team A"],"free_text":false},"handoff":false,"visual_plan":null,"appendix_pages":null,"needs_attention":false,"proposed_answers":null,"open_questions":null}. Never combine ask with human attention controls. After spawning an agent, address its assignment with a live @slug or @agent_id mention in ordinary prose; a name inside backticks does not wake it. A reply_to another agent's message wakes that agent, but only a few times in a row: after four automatic replies with no human message between them, replies stop waking anyone, so use a live @mention or a handoff for anything that still needs an answer. Never reply just to acknowledge; use a reaction. Replies to humans still target them. Do not send acknowledgement-only or status-only messages in response to agent updates; use a reaction when available. A message from a human that is addressed to you, or posted room-wide in your room, always gets a reply, even a one-line one. Silence and reaction-only rules apply to agent-to-agent traffic and to your own unprompted progress reports. A lead with a completed review should publish the home-room summary before any further task-room status. Other free text is always available. Do not send messages outside the given room context.
{"turn_id":"turn_2","agent_id":"agt_2","notes":[{"id":"note_1","from":"usr_1","body":"hi @worker","retry_notice":"check"}],"context":{"role_body":"Be the worker.","rooms":[{"room_id":"room_1"}],"team_roster":[{"id":"agt_2","slug":"ada"}],"you_are":{"id":"agt_2"}},"allowed_tools":["post_message","create_room"]}